course: dictionary
lesson: 13321
title: Grownup and grown-up
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A grownup is a person who is fully grown: an adult, not a child. You can read «Ask a grownup before you use the oven» and know it means an adult who can help you. It is a common word in children's books and safety rules.
explain: Grown-up can also be an adjective. It describes someone or something that acts like an adult: «She gave a grown-up answer to the hard question.» This does not mean she is old. It means her answer was sensible, the way an adult would answer.
explain: You can write grownup as one word or with a hyphen, grown-up. Both are correct. As a noun it has a plural, grownups: «The grownups talked in the kitchen.» Check the job of the word: a noun names a person, and an adjective describes one.
fact: A grownup is an adult, a person who is fully grown.
fact: «Tell a grownup you trust if you feel unsafe.» Grownup is a children's word for an adult.
fact: Grown-up is an adjective meaning adult or acting like an adult, as in «a grown-up decision».
fact: Grownup can be written as one word or with a hyphen: grownup or grown-up.
fact: The plural of grownup is grownups.
exercise: «Ask a grownup before you use the oven.» Who should you ask? | A child your own age | A cat | The oven itself | *An adult who can help you
exercise: «Her grown-up answer surprised everyone.» What does grown-up mean here? | *Sensible, like an adult | Very small | Late for school | Shouted loudly
exercise: What is the plural of grownup? | *grownups | grownuping | grownup | grownupses
test: «Our grownups took us to the zoo on Sunday.» What is a grownup here? | *An adult | A zoo keeper | A type of animal | A child
test: Lily's plan to save money was very grown-up. What does grown-up suggest? | Lost in a shop | Tired and hungry | Silly and loud | *Sensible, like an adult would think
exam: Which sentence uses grown-up as an adjective? | «Tell a grownup.» | *«She made a grown-up choice and saved her money.» | «The grownups sat on the bench.» | «Two grownups came to help.»
